00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,920
We won't let you pass.

264
00:15:50,170 --> 00:15:52,680
What will Tsubasa do?

265
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:58,560
Oh, Tsubasa prepares for his special long-distance shot, the Drive Shot.

266
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:00,270
- Shoot, Tsubasa!
- Tsubasa!

267
00:16:00,310 --> 00:16:02,020
- Tsubasa!
- Shoot!

268
00:16:13,950 --> 00:16:15,370
That goalkeeper...

269
00:16:15,410 --> 00:16:18,830
What's wrong? Tsubasa isn't moving!

270
00:16:18,950 --> 00:16:20,200
Tsubasa?

271
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:22,330
What's wrong, Tsubasa?

272
00:16:23,170 --> 00:16:27,340
Tsubasa also has goal-scoring instincts like a forward.

273
00:16:27,710 --> 00:16:29,250
So he also noticed.

274
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:33,470
That goalkeeper has no weak points.

275
00:16:33,930 --> 00:16:36,680
You feel it right before you shoot.

276
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:39,430
Wherever it goes, he stops it.

277
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:45,190
I've never seen a goalkeeper like him in my life.

278
00:16:45,650 --> 00:16:48,860
Why are you waiting so long? Catch, here it comes!

279
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:53,860
Kaltz makes a tremendous tackle on Tsubasa, who hesitated to shoot.

280
00:16:55,070 --> 00:16:56,700
I can't be afraid now.

281
00:16:56,820 --> 00:16:58,870
Even if I can't find an opening, I must shoot this!

282
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:04,160
Until goalkeeper Dieter Müller's weak point is found...

283
00:17:04,830 --> 00:17:07,840
Until a way to win is found.

284
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,210
Catch!

285
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:12,050
Drive Shot!

286
00:17:12,170 --> 00:17:15,550
Tsubasa takes a deadly Drive Shot!

287
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:18,970
Will it work against this steel giant?

288
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:26,190
Two goalkeepers who stopped Tsubasa's Drive Shot: Wakashimazu and Hernandez.

289
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:31,530
Both stood right on the goal line, so the ball didn't go over their heads.

290
00:17:31,610 --> 00:17:35,240
And when the Drive Shot descended, they stopped it with one hand.

291
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:38,910
Then they placed their other hand behind the ball, close to the goal line.

292
00:17:39,030 --> 00:17:40,870
To prevent it from going into the goal.

293
00:17:40,950 --> 00:17:43,200
A two-stage move.

294
00:17:43,790 --> 00:17:46,500
How will Müller defend?

295
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:52,210
Müller is retreating to the goal line!

296
00:17:52,590 --> 00:17:54,720
He's defending like us!

297
00:17:58,430 --> 00:18:01,140
And he jumps from there!

298
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:03,810
Oh, he makes an arc!

299
00:18:04,390 --> 00:18:11,070
He moves his gigantic arm into the path of the Drive Shot heading toward the goal.

300
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:19,950
And he catches it with one hand!

301
00:18:20,070 --> 00:18:21,580
Great, Müller!

302
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:23,290
Th- This...

303
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:26,040
Müller shocked everyone.

304
00:18:26,290 --> 00:18:28,620
Instead of a two-stage move...

305
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:31,790
He comfortably caught it, like Wakashimazu and Hernandez.

306
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:36,760
He stops Tsubasa's Drive Shot with pure power.

307
00:18:37,130 --> 00:18:38,930
Mü- Müller...

308
00:18:38,970 --> 00:18:42,050
Tsubasa's Drive Shot didn't work either.

309
00:18:42,390 --> 00:18:47,270
He caught the Drive Shot as if it were an ordinary shot.

310
00:18:47,890 --> 00:18:53,770
Dieter Müller. I think he's Europe's number one goalkeeper, not me.

311
00:18:55,530 --> 00:18:57,280
That wasn't bad.

312
00:18:58,610 --> 00:18:59,910
Tsubasa...

313
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:03,870
Well, who's next?

314
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:06,160
What?

315
00:19:06,250 --> 00:19:09,960
Oh, after saving Tsubasa's shot...

316
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:13,040
He throws the ball to the opposing team very comfortably.

317
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:14,800
Mü- Müller?

318
00:19:15,090 --> 00:19:17,800
Damn it! He's mocking us.

319
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:21,930
Nitta from Japan goes to shoot.

320
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:26,100
Take this! Falcon Shot!

321
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:30,390
If I aim for the corner, he's so big that his reaction must be slow.

322
00:19:32,270 --> 00:19:34,400
Useless. He's fast!

323
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:37,400
Müller reacts quickly from left to right.

324
00:19:37,530 --> 00:19:38,900
This is impossible!

325
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:44,780
Such agility thanks to his muscles! Nitta's Falcon Shot doesn't work either.

326
00:19:45,870 --> 00:19:49,910
And again, he throws the ball to the opposing team.

327
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:53,420
I think this is mocking behavior.

328
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:55,880
Bastard. I'll put him in his place.

329
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:56,880
Matsuyama?

330
00:19:57,250 --> 00:20:01,430
Oh, Matsuyama is overlapping from the defense.

331
00:20:01,590 --> 00:20:02,430
Matsuyama!

332
00:20:02,890 --> 00:20:04,550
Tsubasa shot to the top left.

333
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:07,180
And Nitta aimed for the right, it didn't work.

334
00:20:07,970 --> 00:20:10,060
Then I'll shoot to the bottom left.

335
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:11,980
If a goalkeeper is left-handed...

336
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:15,150
The bottom left corner should be the hardest place for him.

337
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:19,570
Take this! Eagle Shot!

338
00:20:22,450 --> 00:20:23,450
There it is!

339
00:20:23,570 --> 00:20:27,030
This is Matsuyama's low long-distance shot, the Eagle Shot!

340
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:29,580
He aimed for the bottom left corner of the goal!

341
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:31,540
Good, be a goal!

342
00:20:33,710 --> 00:20:35,790
Oh, but he caught this too!

343
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:39,050
A difficult spot, but not for him.

344
00:20:39,090 --> 00:20:40,550
Wh- What?

345
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:44,550
Müller throws the ball to the opponent once again.

346
00:20:46,300 --> 00:20:47,810
He's messing with us.

347
00:20:47,970 --> 00:20:49,560
Bastard!

348
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:51,890
This time Soda overlaps.

349
00:20:51,980 --> 00:20:57,650
The Japan team, angered by Müller's attitude, attacks fiercely.

350
00:20:57,730 --> 00:20:59,860
If a straight shot doesn't work, how about one with spin?

351
00:20:59,940 --> 00:21:02,950
Sharp Shot!

352
00:21:03,030 --> 00:21:04,820
This is Soda's spinning shot!

353
00:21:04,910 --> 00:21:08,160
The Sharp Shot curved violently to the right.

354
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:09,830
This time, the far bottom right corner.

355
00:21:11,950 --> 00:21:15,960
And Hyuga is heading to the same spot.

356
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:17,750
Great accompaniment, Hyuga.

357
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:20,210
Just what's expected from Japan's best forward!

358
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:23,220
If Müller can't hold this shot with his palm and punches it away...

359
00:21:23,510 --> 00:21:26,470
Then Hyuga can easily strike the loose ball afterward.

360
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:43,780
He...

361
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:47,110
He stopped it with just his left hand!

362
00:21:47,410 --> 00:21:48,200
What!?

363
00:21:48,530 --> 00:21:52,330
Hyuga shoots incredibly powerfully from close range, but still...

364
00:21:52,450 --> 00:21:55,750
Müller stops it with just his left hand.

365
00:21:56,370 --> 00:21:58,210
What a strong arm!

366
00:21:58,670 --> 00:22:00,750
Now I understand why they call him...

367
00:22:01,130 --> 00:22:03,880
The Steel Giant Dieter Müller.

368
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:50,010
Next Episode: Schneider vs. Wakabayashi